# Diagnostic environment v5: read the backup partition array at its real LBA.
#
# v4 dumped LBA 0xeaa7fe -- "one before the last LBA", the usual place for a
# backup array -- and got zeros, because I assumed the location instead of
# reading it out of the header. The backup header at 0xeaa7ff says
# pte_lba = 0xeaa7fb, three LBAs earlier: 32 entries x 128 bytes = 4096 bytes =
# exactly one 4 KiB block, and the two blocks after it are unused padding. That
# is why 0xeaa7fe was empty.
#
# Two fields in that header disagree with the primary, and they are the reason
# this is worth another round:
#   disk GUID ends 0x13 in the primary header, 0xf3 in the backup
#   pte_crc    0x7ae21393 primary, 0x7ae2f393 backup
# If those are real and not OCR noise, the backup array describes a *different*
# partition table than the primary -- which would mean the fourteen partitions
# U-Boot sees are a rewritten table and the original layout still sits at the
# end of the LUN. Loaders that cross-check primary against backup, or that fall
# back to the backup, would resolve names like boot that the primary no longer
# contains. Everything hinges on what those 32 slots actually hold, so this
# image prints the name of entries 1..16 (16 bytes each, UTF-16LE, so md's ASCII
# column spells eight characters) plus entry 1's starting LBA.
#
# Also closes two gaps from v4: the second partition on LUN1 and the first on
# LUN3 (LUN3 turned out to be ALIGN_TO_128K_1 / cdt / ddr, a Qualcomm ddr+c d t
# LUN; LUN1 holds xbl). Read-only, as always.
bootdelay=2
bootretry=-1

stdin=serial,button-kbd
stdout=serial,vidconsole
stderr=serial,vidconsole

preboot=echo; echo RMX1971 diag v5

# Small LUNs: the two entries v4's photo cut off.
diag_small=setenv n;setenv s;setenv z;part name scsi 1 2 n;part start scsi 1 2 s;part size scsi 1 2 z;echo L1.2=$n,$s,$z;setenv n;setenv s;setenv z;part name scsi 3 1 n;part start scsi 3 1 s;part size scsi 3 1 z;echo L3.1=$n,$s,$z

# Primary array (LBA 2) entry 1 name, as the control.
diag_prim=scsi dev 0;scsi read 0xa0000000 2 1;md.b 0xa0000038 16

# Backup array at the LBA the backup header names.
diag_bak=scsi dev 0;scsi read 0xa0000000 0xeaa7fb 1;md.b 0xa0000020 8;md.b 0xa0000038 16;md.b 0xa00000b8 16;md.b 0xa0000138 16;md.b 0xa00001b8 16;md.b 0xa0000238 16;md.b 0xa00002b8 16;md.b 0xa0000338 16;md.b 0xa00003b8 16;md.b 0xa0000438 16;md.b 0xa00004b8 16;md.b 0xa0000538 16;md.b 0xa00005b8 16;md.b 0xa0000638 16;md.b 0xa00006b8 16;md.b 0xa0000738 16;md.b 0xa00007b8 16

bootcmd=echo === small;run diag_small;echo === primary pte1;run diag_prim;echo === backup array;run diag_bak;echo === end;sleep 40;reset
